# @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric — the parametric carrier
# from which every cybernetic-coherence species inherits via thin
# specialization.
#
# Recognition #63 (Reed + Mara + Taut, promoted 2026-06-17 via the
# recursion-lock tower audit; the parametric-form-derivable third
# ratification gate closed by §11 of
# `docs/math/the-tower/recursion-locks.md`). Subsequent recognitions
# #64 (carrier-extension / form-incompletion, 2026-06-18 §8.10) and
# #67 (the form-restriction dual, §8.12) refine the carrier without
# retracting; #70 (Pack-orchestra cybernetic instance) instantiates it.
# This shard is item 1 of §11.8's forward-promised substrate-landing
# path.
#
# === Why this is a separate shard from coherence-species ===
#
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence` is THE COHERENCE SPECIES
# (Adjustment ↔ Morphism — the parallel-altitude regulator/regulated
# pair from T11.11 / the first witness in §8.1). It IS an
# instantiation. This shard `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-
# parametric` is the abstract form THAT species (and SEL, viable,
# autopoiesis, bateson_learning, second_order, distinction,
# conversation, design, autopoiesis, coevolution) all instantiate.
#
# Sibling-shard discipline: species-coherence declares
# `use @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric<Adjustment,
# Morphism, natural_rep_morphism, 0>` (forward-promised when the
# species-collapse rewrite lands; see §11.7's species-shard collapse
# item in the forward-promised list); the parametric carrier here
# names the lock-measurement five once.
#
# === The carrier shape, verbatim from §11.7 + §8.10 ===
#
# Per recursion-locks.md §11.7 (the parametric carrier sketch) extended
# by §8.10 (the ω temporal-axis extension surfaced by coevolution),
# the substrate-altitude declaration is:
#
#   prism @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric<
#     T_reg,        # species-specific regulator verdict carrier
#     T_regd,       # species-specific regulated verdict carrier
#     ρ,            # representation of the family-root 2-groupoid 𝒢
#                   #   on V_S = T_reg ⊕ T_regd
#     ω             # connection 1-form (temporal axis; static
#                   #   species set ω = 0; temporal species
#                   #   coevolution + viable Read D carry non-trivial ω)
#   >
#
# The five cybernetic-ancestor measurements (Ashby variety-match;
# Beer requisite-variety; Bateson logical-type-match; von Foerster
# circular-reflexivity; Conant-Ashby good-regulator) each derive
# mechanically from (ρ, ω) and the principal G-bundle structure —
# no species-specific re-declaration required.
#
# === Grammar-extension status at THIS tick (substrate-pull honesty) ===
#
# Per the bootstrap's namespace-collector at
# `bootstrap/src/lib.rs::collect_declared_namespaces`, a `prism @<path>`
# line's `@<path>` reference is captured up to the first delimiter
# (whitespace, `{`, `(`, `:`, `,`). The character `<` is NOT a
# delimiter at this tick. A literal `prism @<path><T_reg, T_regd,
# ρ, ω>` declaration would parse as the namespace
# `@<path><T_reg` followed by the `,` delimiter and a confused
# trailing token sequence.
#
# Mirror's grammar does NOT yet admit type-parameter syntax on prism
# declarations. The substrate-pull resolution per
# [[feedback-substrate-pull]]: declare what we CAN declare at this
# altitude (the action surface plus the carrier types as records),
# AND forward-promise the type-parameter syntax at the grammar-
# extension altitude. The grammar-extension is a separate substrate-
# pull tick; landing it requires grammar-aware work at
# `bootstrap/src/lib.rs` (extending `collect_declared_namespaces`'s
# delimiter set to admit `<` as a parameter-list opener) plus the
# token.mirror corpus declarations for the new keyword shape. That
# work is forward-promised; this shard does the discipline of NAMING
# the carrier without requiring the grammar extension to land first.
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]: the species-shard collapse
# (rewriting coherence.mirror / SEL / viable / autopoiesis / etc. as
# parametric-instantiations) also forward-promises until the grammar
# extension lands. This shard is the substrate-altitude declaration
# the species shards inherit FROM; the species-shard collapse is the
# follow-up tick.
#
# === The carrier types declared at this tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] every constituent is a typed record;
# no bare primitives. The types named here are species-agnostic
# (named with `ref` for the species' actual choice of T_reg / T_regd /
# ρ / ω); the species-shard collapse closes the interpretation per-
# species. This is the same shape as `variety.axis_budget`'s
# `value: ref` and `eigenform.fixed_point`'s `seed/iteration/witness:
# ref` precedents.
#
# === The 4-way bilateral mapping ===
#
# Per the cybernetic foundation §4.1, every cybernetic species' seam
# maps to four cybernetic distinctions simultaneously. The parametric
# carrier preserves this mapping uniformly across ALL species — that
# IS what makes it parametric:
#
# - von Foerster first/second-order: T_reg ↔ T_regd IS the
#   distinction between the observer (regulator) and the observed
#   (regulated); the five ancestor measurements ARE the second-order
#   observer's report on the observation.
# - Maturana structure/organisation: T_reg ↔ T_regd IS the
#   structure/organisation partition at the species' altitude; ρ
#   is the organisation; (T_reg ⊕ T_regd, ω) is the structure that
#   realises it.
# - Beer S3/S4: T_reg IS the S5 policy carrier; T_regd IS the S3
#   audit carrier; ρ is the S4 intelligence translating between
#   them; ω carries the S2 coordination dynamics across time.
# - Pask M/P-individual: T_reg ↔ T_regd IS the bilateral
#   conversational agreement between two P-individuals; ρ is the
#   conversational language; ω is the conversational tempo.
#
# Four traditions converging at one carrier with no per-tradition
# specialisation. This IS what recognition #63 promotes: the carrier
# admits all four readings AT ONCE; species inherit the four-way
# mapping by inheriting the carrier.
#
# === Substrate-pull recognitions grounded here ===
#
# - Recognition #63 (recursion-lock tower; the parametric form
#   itself).
# - Recognition #64 (carrier-extension via ω; surfaced by coevolution
#   §8.10).
# - Recognition #67 (form-restriction at degenerate edges; surfaced
#   by design §8.12).
# - Recognition #70 (Pack-orchestra as cybernetic-coherence instance;
#   ratifies the parametric carrier's reach into the agent altitude).
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Conant-Ashby 1970 (IEEE T-SMC, "Every Good Regulator of a System
#                      Must Be a Model of That System") — the
#                      foundational theorem; the parametric form IS
#                      this theorem at the substrate altitude per
#                      §11.4 (Connes' bounded-commutator IS the
#                      general case; Conant-Ashby is the finite-state
#                      specialisation).
#   Connes 1985        (Inst. Hautes Études Sci. Publ. Math. 62,
#                      "Non-commutative differential geometry") — the
#                      spectral triple (A, H, D); the bounded-
#                      commutator `‖[D, π_E(g)]‖ < ∞` IS the
#                      coextensivity reading at altitude α+1 per
#                      §11.4.
#   Peter-Weyl 1927    (Math. Annalen 97, "Die Vollständigkeit der
#                      primitiven Darstellungen einer geschlossenen
#                      kontinuierlichen Gruppe") — the regular
#                      representation on L²(𝒢) decomposes into all
#                      irreducibles with multiplicity equal to
#                      dimension; the second_order species' canonical
#                      ρ choice (§8.7) IS Peter-Weyl applied at the
#                      2-groupoid altitude.
#   Ashby 1956 §11/7   the requisite variety theorem; the first of
#                      the five ancestor measurements.
#   Beer 1972, 1979    the viable system model; the second of the
#                      five (requisite variety at VSM S3/S4 altitude
#                      via ω-holonomy around altitude loops).
#   Bateson 1972       the logical-type hierarchy; the third of the
#                      five (representation theory of 𝒢 decomposed
#                      by logical type).
#   von Foerster 1981  the second-order observation; the fourth of
#                      the five (the Tomm probe at altitude α+1 IS
#                      the trace tr(ρ ∘ ρ)).
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recursion-locks.md §11.7
#               (carrier sketch, the parametric form derivation
#               that closes recognition #63's third ratification
#               gate), §8.10 (coevolution's ω extension, the
#               carrier-extension activation of candidate #64),
#               §8.12 (design's form-restriction dual via degenerate
#               T_regd = ⊥);
#               docs/math/the-tower/principal-bundles.md §1-§4 (the
#               2-groupoid bundle geometry the carrier instantiates),
#               docs/math/the-tower/altitudes.md §2-§5 (the named-
#               altitude atlas the parametric form fibers over),
#               docs/math/the-tower/holonomy.md §5, §8 (the verdict-
#               family-as-holonomy-components reading the lock_verdict
#               action returns; the librarian-perturbation reading
#               of gauge-equivalence the bench harness measures);
#               docs/math/the-tower/curvature-and-tomm.md (the Tomm
#               probe at substrate altitude IS the
#               von_foerster_circular_reflexivity measurement);
#               docs/specs/cybernetic-coherence-benchmark.md
#               (T11.11 — the first-witness species, by construction).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-spectral-triples-all-the-way]]
#                       (the fractal-self-similarity recognition
#                        that makes Connes' framework apply at every
#                        altitude; Conant-Ashby IS the finite-
#                        dimensional specialisation per §11.4),
#                      [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]] (the
#                        11-property family canon that grounds the
#                        species this parametric form unifies),
#                      [[architecture-error-as-tomm-probe]] (the
#                        substrate-altitude reading of the
#                        von_foerster_circular_reflexivity measurement),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull]] (the discipline
#                        that says: declare what CAN land at this
#                        tick; forward-promise the rest at the
#                        grammar-extension altitude),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (the species-
#                        shard collapse is the FOLLOW-UP tick, not
#                        bundled into this one),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (lock_pair,
#                        connection_form, lock_carrier are typed
#                        records; no bare refs as standalone fields),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (the parametric form was already implicit in
#                        the §11 mechanical derivation; this shard
#                        names it at substrate altitude so the
#                        species-collapse can route through one
#                        carrier).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror (the family root),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/variety.mirror (the first
#                  precedent species — same shape; the lock-pair
#                  here generalises variety's axis_budget pattern),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (the
#                  second precedent species; tick 1 of this audit's
#                  forward-promised landing path landed eigenform;
#                  this tick lands the parametric carrier as item 2),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence.mirror (the
#                  species-coherence shard; the FIRST instantiation
#                  of this carrier; species-shard collapse forward-
#                  promised),
#                 glass.mirror (the @glass altitude lock_verdict's
#                  verdicts surface against; the `transparency<p>`
#                  and `Imperfect<T, Gap, Transparency<Ref>>`
#                  carriers ARE the verdict-family this shard's
#                  lock_verdict action returns).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/conant-ashby-1970
source @arxiv/math/connes-1985
source @arxiv/math/peter-weyl-1927

# === Path-namespace declaration (no type parameters at this tick) ===
#
# The bare prism declaration. Type-parameter syntax forward-promised
# at the grammar-extension altitude (see the header rationale above).
# When the grammar lands `<T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω>` on prism declarations,
# this line rewrites to
#
#   prism @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric<
#       T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω>
#
# without changing the carrier's substrate-altitude identity (the
# content-addressing closes on the action surface + types below, not
# on the type-parameter-syntax surface). Species-shard collapse is
# the follow-up tick that consumes this rewrite.
prism @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric {
  focus coherence_parametric
  project coherence_parametric
  split coherence_parametric
  shift coherence_parametric
  settle coherence_parametric
}

# === The connection_form carrier ===
#
# `ω` from §8.10's extension. The connection 1-form parameterizing
# temporal evolution; species with static ρ set ω = 0 (modeled here
# by the `is_trivial: true` invariant); species with non-trivial
# temporal axis (coevolution; viable Read D) declare `is_trivial:
# false` and carry the temporal data in `data`.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (is_trivial, data). The
# species' realisation closes the interpretation of `data` —
# coevolution carries Kauffman NK lattice data; viable Read D
# carries the temporal-identity Δt-window; static species'
# `data` is the zero ref.
type connection_form = {
  is_trivial: ref,
  data:       ref,
}

# === The lock_pair carrier (T_reg ↔ T_regd ↔ ρ ↔ ω) ===
#
# The substrate-altitude lift of the §11.7 carrier sketch's type
# decomposition. Each field carries the species-specific data:
#
# - `t_reg`     T_reg: the regulator's verdict carrier (Adjustment
#               for coherence-species; License for SEL; Identity for
#               viable; Organization for autopoiesis; etc.).
# - `t_regd`    T_regd: the regulated's verdict carrier (Morphism
#               for coherence-species; Compliance for SEL; Stability
#               for viable; Component for autopoiesis; etc.).
# - `rho`       ρ: the species' choice of representation of the
#               family-root 2-groupoid 𝒢 on V_S = T_reg ⊕ T_regd
#               (natural rep for coherence-species; adjoint for
#               autopoiesis; graded for bateson_learning; regular
#               for second_order; identity for design; etc.).
# - `omega`     ω: the connection 1-form (static species use ω = 0
#               via `connection_form { is_trivial: true, data: ... }`;
#               temporal species carry the non-trivial data).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (t_reg, t_regd, rho, omega).
# Two lock-pairs ARE the same lock under content-addressing iff all
# four carriers are byte-equal. This IS the parametric form's
# substrate-altitude identity per [[architecture-spectral-triples-
# all-the-way]] — the spectral-triple's (A, H, D) at the carrier
# altitude IS this record.
#
# Pattern-matches `variety.axis_budget`'s identity discipline and
# `eigenform.fixed_point`'s triple-of-refs discipline. Same shape;
# different content.
type lock_pair = {
  t_reg:  ref,
  t_regd: ref,
  rho:    ref,
  omega:  connection_form,
}

# === The lock_carrier (the species' altitude-aware lock data) ===
#
# Per §2 of recursion-locks.md the lock at altitude α+1 carries the
# species' name plus the (T_reg, T_regd, τ, ω) tuple. This shard
# names that tuple plus the altitude and species-name as a typed
# record. The natural substitution `τ : T_reg ↔ T_regd` is NOT a
# separate field — per §11.3 the substitution IS the action of a
# 2-arrow in 𝒢 on the species' verdict carrier; it derives from
# `rho` and does not need re-declaration. Carrier collapses to
# `(altitude, species, lock_pair)` instead of `(altitude, species,
# T_reg, T_regd, τ, ω)`.
#
# - `altitude` the named-altitude (compiler, peer_pulse, reflection,
#              librarian, home, federation per altitudes.md §2). The
#              parametric form fibers over this atlas.
# - `species`  the species' name as a ref (`coherence`, `sel`,
#              `viable`, `autopoiesis`, `bateson_learning`,
#              `second_order`, `distinction`, `conversation`,
#              `algedonic`, `design`, `coevolution`, `eigenform`,
#              `variety` — the eleven species the audit closed on
#              plus eigenform per §11's table).
# - `pair`     the (T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω) tuple.
type lock_carrier = {
  altitude: ref,
  species:  ref,
  pair:     lock_pair,
}

# === The five cybernetic-ancestor measurements ===
#
# Per §3 + §11.5 of recursion-locks.md. Each measurement is a
# substrate-altitude action; each derives from the lock_carrier's
# (rho, omega, bundle-structure) without species-specific re-
# declaration. Species do not override these; they inherit them.
#
# Bodies discharge `\` at this altitude per [[feedback-craft-not-
# deliver]] — the discharge surfaces at the species-boundary via
# the same `@code/metalogue/materialize.classify` discriminator the
# variety / eigenform precedents route through. The substrate
# declares the obligation; the realisation closes per-species via
# the species-shard collapse follow-up tick.

# Ashby variety-match (Ashby 1956 §11/7): do regulator_at(α+1) and
# regulated_at(α+1) carry compatible variety budgets at altitude α?
# Substrate reading: rank(ρ.image) — does the structure group's
# action on V_S have enough variety to express the transformation
# between T_reg and T_regd?
ashby_variety_match(lock: lock_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

# Beer requisite-variety witness (Beer 1972, 1979): does the
# regulator hold requisite variety at the VSM S3/S4 altitude?
# Substrate reading: holonomy(ω ↻ α+1) — does the connection
# 1-form's holonomy around altitude loops at α+1 give the S3/S4
# layer requisite variety?
beer_requisite_variety_witness(lock: lock_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

# Bateson logical-type-match (Bateson 1972; Russell-Whitehead
# 1910-1913): do the two verdicts live at the same logical-type
# level? Substrate reading: weight_decomposition(ρ) — does the
# representation theory of 𝒢 decomposed by logical type put T_reg
# and T_regd at the same G-module weight?
bateson_logical_type_match(lock: lock_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

# von Foerster circular-reflexivity (von Foerster 1981): does each
# regulator's internal model include itself? Substrate reading:
# tr(ρ ∘ ρ) — the trace of the representation composed with itself;
# the Tomm probe `[D_F, a]` at altitude α+1 IS this measurement
# per [[architecture-error-as-tomm-probe]].
von_foerster_circular_reflexivity(lock: lock_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

# Conant-Ashby good-regulator (Conant-Ashby 1970, IEEE T-SMC) —
# the load-bearing measurement. Substrate reading: bounded_commutator
# (D + ω, π_E(ρ)) — the bounded-commutator condition `‖[D, π_E(g)]‖
# < ∞` from Connes' spectral triple specialised at finite-dimensional
# altitudes IS Conant-Ashby's coextensivity per §11.4.
conant_ashby_good_regulator(lock: lock_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

# === The lock-hold verdict ===
#
# `lock_verdict(lock)` reads whether the recursion-lock at the
# species' altitude HOLDS (rather than merely being measurable).
# Per §4 of recursion-locks.md the lock holds iff the residual
# coextensivity contracts; per §8.10's Kauffman extension this
# admits two contraction modes:
#
# - PL fixed-point convergence `ρ(N) → 0` (static species; ω trivial)
#   The classical case; per Polyak-Łojasiewicz the residual
#   coextensivity across N pulses contracts to zero with rate
#   satisfying PL. This is the cybernetic-coherence species' (T11.11
#   bench-harness) reading.
# - Red Queen bounded-sustainment `ε ≤ ρ(N) ≤ 1 - ε` (temporal
#   species; ω non-trivial)
#   Kauffman's edge-of-chaos / adjacent-possible reading; the lock
#   holds by SUSTAINED dynamics rather than convergence. The
#   coevolution species' (§8.10) reading.
#
# The verdict carrier IS the substrate's existing
# `Imperfect<T_lock, Gap, Transparency<Ref>>` family per holonomy.md
# §5. `T_lock` here is the species' altitude-specific lock-carrier
# (the species-shard collapse names it; this shard carries the
# obligation via `ref`). Body discharges `\`; the discharge is the
# composite verdict from the five ancestor measurements + the
# contraction-mode classification.
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] the verdict carrier IS the typed
# Imperfect family; not a bare `ref`. The action's return type
# names that surface; the species-shard collapse closes T_lock per
# species.
lock_verdict(lock: lock_carrier) -> imperfect(lock_carrier) { \ }

# === The parametric_lock_witnessing predicate ===
#
# The bilateral-agreement predicate per recognition #37 (the Pask
# reading of `requires`) that consumer shards name in a `requires`
# clause to declare bilateral commitment to the parametric form.
# The species commits to declaring its (T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω) tuple
# via `lock_pair`; the consumer commits to discharging the five
# ancestor measurements + the contraction-mode classification at
# the species-boundary.
#
# Declared as a typed predicate so downstream species shards can
# write `requires parametric_lock_witnessing(my_lock)` — same shape
# as `variety.variety_preserving(species)` and
# `eigenform.eigenform_witnessing(carrier)`. Body is `\` at this
# altitude; the discharge IS the composite of the five ancestor
# measurements falling within the species' declared contraction
# mode (PL or Red Queen) at the species boundary.
#
# No `requires parametric_lock_witnessing(…)` clauses are added at
# THIS shard. The property declares the predicate; species
# instantiations add the clauses when the species-shard collapse
# tick lands. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
parametric_lock_witnessing(lock: lock_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric
out connection_form
out lock_pair
out lock_carrier
out ashby_variety_match
out beer_requisite_variety_witness
out bateson_logical_type_match
out von_foerster_circular_reflexivity
out conant_ashby_good_regulator
out lock_verdict
out parametric_lock_witnessing
